
Nox Security Assessment

1 issue needs attention (1 finding).
  1. Untrusted input reaches an LLM prompt (prompt injection) at src/routes/assistant.js:9 (high severity, medium confidence).

Checks completed: secrets, application code, dependencies (123 packages), infrastructure configuration, AI integrations, sensitive-data handling, supply chain and authorization (Express routes; leads only).

Not determined by this scan:
  - Exploitability: the finding was neither confirmed exploitable nor shown to be prevented; it is a potential issue.

Additional verification recommended:
  - Runtime testing for src/routes/assistant.js:9 (TAINT-AI-001): 2 attack hypotheses (PI-DIRECT, PI-INDIRECT), e.g. make the model obey an instruction supplied through untrusted input.
  - Authorization: GET /api/invoices/:id (src/routes/invoices.js:14) loads a record by a caller-supplied id with no visible ownership check. Test it with two user accounts: request user A's record while signed in as user B.

Next steps:
  - Plan the runtime tests (offline, sends nothing): nox attack plan . --findings ./findings.json
  - Record a reviewed, accepted risk as a waiver: nox vex init --input ./findings.json
  - Catch new issues before they are committed: nox install-hook
